{{also|Minute|minuté|minutë|minutė|minutę|minūte|minūtē}}

==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=time|:inh|enm:mynute}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mynute}}, {{m|enm|minute}}, {{m|enm|mynet}}, from {{der|en|fro|minute}}, from {{der|en|la-med|minūta|t=60th of an hour; note}}. {{doublet|en|menu|menudo}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|mĭn'ĭt}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪnɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-a minute.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-minute-noun.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪnɪt|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q7727}} A [[unit]] of [[time]] which is one sixtieth of an [[hour]] (sixty [[second#English:_Q11574|second]]s).
#: {{alti|en|mul:min<id:Q7727><qq:least ambiguous symbol>|;|mul:m<id:Q7727>|mul:M<id:Q7727><qq:symbols also widely used>}}
#: {{hol|en|hectosecond<id:Q1040427>|<|kilosecond<id:Q1374438>|<|hour<id:Q25235>|<|day<id:Q573>|<|week<id:Q23387>|<|megasecond<id:Q1197459>|<|fortnight<id:Q2993680>|<|month<id:Q5151>|<|year<id:Q577>|<|gigasecond<id:Q1377051>|<|century<id:Q578>|<|kiloannum<id:Q3013059>|kiloyear<id:Q3013059>|millennium<id:Q36507>|<|terasecond<id:Q1322380>|<|mega-annum<id:Q20764>|megayear<id:Q20764>|<|petasecond<id:Q1066138>|<|giga-annum<id:Q524410>|gigayear<id:Q524410>|<|exasecond<id:Q906223>|<|zettasecond<id:Q12011178>|<|yottasecond<id:Q14913554>|<|ronnasecond<id:Q122972375>|<|quettasecond<id:Q116939356>}}
#: {{mer|en|quectosecond<id:Q125387265>|<|rontosecond<id:Q125387281>|<|yoctosecond<id:Q2762458>|<|zeptosecond<id:Q1872619>|<|attosecond<id:Q2483628>|<|femtosecond<id:Q1777507>|<|picosecond<id:Q3902709>|<|nanosecond<id:Q838801>|<|microsecond<id:Q842015>|<|millisecond<id:Q723733>|<|centisecond<id:Q3249364>|<|decisecond<id:Q3251645>|<|second<id:Q11574>|<|decasecond<id:Q1040401>}}
#: {{ux|en|You have twenty '''minutes''' to complete the test.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kristen Rogers|title=Want to live an extra 5 to 10 years? Adopt this habit, study suggests|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/15/health/physical-activity-extend-life-expectancy-wellness|date=2024-11-15|passage=Total activity levels in the lowest quartile were equivalent to walking for 49 '''minutes''' at roughly 3 miles (4.8 kilometers) per hour daily. Total activity levels in the second-, third- and fourth-highest quartiles were equivalent to 78, 105 and 160 minutes, respectively.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250711034836/https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/15/health/physical-activity-extend-life-expectancy-wellness}}
# {{senseid|en|short but unspecified time, a moment}} {{lb|en|informal}} A [[short]] but unspecified [[time]] period.
#: {{syn|en|instant|jiffy|mo|moment|sec|second|tic|Thesaurus:moment}}
#: {{coi|en|give me a '''minute'''}}
#: {{ux|en|Wait a '''minute''', I’m not ready yet!}}
# {{senseid|en|Q209426}}A unit of [[angle]] equal to one-sixtieth of a [[degree]].
#: {{syn|en|minute of arc|sexagesm|arcminute}}
#: {{ux|en|We need to be sure these maps are accurate to within one '''minute''' of arc.
}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly in the plural|[[minutes]]}} A (usually formal) written record of a meeting or a part of a meeting.
#: {{ux|en|Let’s look at the '''minutes''' of last week’s meeting.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Pink Dandelion|title=The Quakers: A Very Short Introduction|page=52
|passage=The Clerk or 'recording Clerk' drafts a '''minute''' and then, or at a later time, reads it to the Meeting. Subsequent contributions are on the wording of the '''minute''' only, until it can be accepted by the Meeting. Once the '''minute''' is accepted, the Meeting moves on to the next item on the agenda.}}
# A unit of purchase on a [[telephone]] or other similar [[network]], especially a [[cell phone]] network, roughly equivalent in [[gross]] form to sixty seconds' use of the network.
#: {{ux|en|If you buy this model, you’ll get 100 free '''minutes'''.}}
# A point in time; a moment.
#: {{syn|en|instant|moment|Thesaurus:point in time}}
#: {{ux|en|I [[conked out]] the '''minute''' I got home.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aureng-zebe|passage=Tell her, that I some Certainty may bring; / I go this '''minute''' to attend the king.}}
# A [[nautical]] or a [[geographic]] [[mile]].
# An old [[coin]], a [[half]] [[farthing]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A very small part of anything, or anything very small; a jot; a whit.
#* {{RQ:Taylor Ductor Dubitantium|volume=1|chapter=Of the Probable or Thinking Conscience.|passage={{...}}according to the Prophecies of him, which were so clear and descended to '''minutes''' and circumstances of his passion}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} A fixed part of a [[module]].
# {{lb|en|slang|US|Canada|dialectal}} A [[while]] or a long unspecified period of time.
#: {{syn|en|age|spell|Thesaurus:eon}}
#: {{ux|en|Oh, I ain't heard that song in a '''minute'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Kenneth Ring|title=Letters from Palestine|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=sLMRHc1aqSIC&lpg=PA18|page=18
|passage=“Man, I haven’t seen you in a '''minute''',” he says, smiling still. “Maybe like two, three years ago?”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|site=Complex.com|date=June 10 2010|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2010/06/lil-b-talks-getting-sucker-punched-gay-rumors-drake-envy|author=w:Lil B|passage=I seen {{w|Too$hort}} up there. Me and $hort ain't talked in a '''minute'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528035851/https://www.complex.com/music/2010/06/lil-b-talks-getting-sucker-punched-gay-rumors-drake-envy|archivedate=28 May 2023}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=2016-11-08|director=Ben Katai|writer=Ben Katai; Josh Corbin; Sharon Lennon|medium=TV|series=w:StartUp (TV series)|season=1|number=10|title=StartUp(Recapitalization)|actor=w:Edi Gathegi|role=Ronald Dacey|url=https://tvshowtranscripts.ourboard.org/viewtopic.php?f=705&t=28573|text=RON:I remember my first. I was a '''minute''' younger than you. {{...}}I remember thinking, saying to myself..."This is the first time I'm eating as a person who killed someone."}}
# The distance that can be traveled in a minute.

